ing."]}, "overview": "Colorado's eighth district is a genuinely even seat, and first-term Republican Gabe Evans is defending it against Democrat Manny Rutinel in a favorable midterm climate for Democrats. Ten expert ratings place the race between Tossup and Likely Democratic, with most calling it Lean Democratic, and prediction markets price a Democratic win at roughly 84 percent. The only public poll, a Republican-sponsored survey from mid-September, showed Evans ahead by two points, but it is dated and partisan.\n\nRutinel has raised more money than Evans and holds a cash advantage, while Democratic outside groups have outspent Republican ones by a wide margin. Headlines show Evans working to distance himself from an unpopular president while Rutinel campaigns against that agenda, with Latino voters seen as decisive. The race points to a narrow Democratic win of about six points, with meaningful uncertainty given thin polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7882, "margin": 4.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7652, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7649, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7806, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7027, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6862, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7621, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7968, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7638, "margin": 4.3}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7725, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7967, "margin": 4.6}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8011, "margin": 4.6}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8034, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7177, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7479, "margin": 4.7}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7209, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7925, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.7716, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.